    "summary": {
      "PREAMBLE": "Rambilash Banarsasi Yadav vs The State Of Maharashtra on 30\nJanuary, 2024\n\nAuthor: Sarang V. Kotwal\nBench: Sarang V. Kotwal\n2024:Bhc-As:5106\n Gokhale 1 of 3 \n In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay\n Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction\n Anticipatory Bail Application No. 177 Of 2023\n Rambilash Banarasi Yadav ..\n Versus\n State of Maharashtra ..\n__ __ __\n Mr. Anup Lahoti for Applicant.\n\n Ms. Mahalakshmi Ganapathy, App for State/Respondent.\n___ _ _\n_\n Coram : Sarang V. Kotwal, J.\nDate : 30 January 2024 P.C. :\n1.\n The Applicant is seeking anticipatory bail in connection with C.R.No.837 of 2022,\nregistered at Pelhar Police Station, Mira Bhayandar, on 03.10.2022, under section 328 of the Indian Penal Code and under sections 26(2), 4 and 30(2)(e) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (hereinafter referred to as 'FSS Act').\n2.\n",
      "facts": "They were carrying banned articles namely 'Gutka'.\nAt about 12.15p.m.\nboth the trucks were intercepted.\nThe search of those trucks was taken.\nHe had ordered some of the goods.\n\nHe gave the name of the present applicant as the person who was getting those goods from one Arjunsingh for sale in Maharashtra.\n",
      "arguments": "Section 328 of the I.P.C. is not attracted.\nThe applicant is falsely implicated in this case.\n",
      "ANALYSIS": "These offences are of the similar nature.\nThe observations in that order are squarely applicable to the facts and arguments on behalf of the applicant in the present case.\nThere are similar antecedents against him.\n",
      "decision": "As far as the applicability of Section 328 of the I.P.C. is concerned, this Court, vide the order dated 30.01.2024 passed in A.B.A.No.207 of 2024 has dealt with this issue.\nThere is definite material against the applicant.\nThe offence is serious.\nThe applicant's custodial interrogation is necessary.\nConsidering all these aspects, the applicant cannot be protected.\n\n7. The application is rejected.\n"
